# Print-in-place fit proofs. `fitcheck` renders every moving/fixed pairwise
# interference — both spinner rotors vs the card+posts, the bead vs the card,
# the hinge pin vs card and flap, and the easel flap vs the card at 0/35/70 deg
# and at the deployed angle — and must be EMPTY (all clearances real on the
# built mesh). `fitcheck_neg` over-rotates the flap past its designed stop and
# MUST interfere: it proves the rotation stop exists AND that the check can
# fail. The bead's breakaway anchor nib is a declared weld (CC2) drawn outside
# the fitcheck bodies — see NOTES.md.
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
